      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "From my testing, the reference camera's layer mask is completely ignored by VRC...  The only layer that is not visible on the eye camera(s) is MirrorReflect, and that's only visible in mirrors.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-01-13T07:19:16.256Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In worlds with custom layer setups, some objects that are meant to be hidden on layers are visible in the photo camera.  This is prominently displayed in worlds like the MMD Dance Stage and MMD Nightclub, which both make extensive use of layers to hide their \"stages\" except in mirrors or render target cameras.\n\nThe photo camera presumably controls some layers itself for its various effects, so the reference camera should not be able to dictate all of the photo camera's layer settings, but it should at least be able to inherit some of the custom reference camera layer settings. Alternatively, there could be settings in the VRCWorld descriptor to specify the layers of the photo camera independent of the reference camera.",
